Summary:
During today’s session, we continued enhancing the frontend design of the Developer Portfolio Evaluator to make the interface more structured and visually appealing. Improvements were made to layout, spacing, and presentation to ensure a better user experience. Alongside the UI enhancements, we were introduced to database integration and began working with MongoDB. The initial setup for connecting the backend with MongoDB was explored, and basic understanding of storing data in a database was developed. This marked the transition from a purely functional application to one that can persist data.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, the frontend design showed noticeable improvement in terms of usability and visual structure. Additionally, we gained foundational knowledge of MongoDB and how it can be integrated with a Node.js backend. The setup for database connectivity was initiated, preparing the project for data storage capabilities. This expanded the scope of the application from real-time evaluation to potential data persistence. Overall, the session strengthened both UI development skills and introduced backend data management concepts.
